<title>USA: H.K. firm cuts Action Performance stake.</title>
<headline>H.K. firm cuts Action Performance stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>CMC Enterprises Ltd, a Hong Kong-based investment firm, said Thursday it cut its stake in Action Performance Companies Inc. to 500,000 common shares, or 3.8 percent of the total outstanding, from 999,000 shares, or 7.6 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, CMC said it sold 499,000 shares between August 15 and December 5, 1996 at prices ranging from $12.50 to $17.125 a share.</p>
